{"tool_name":"em-dat","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:em-dat"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"EM-DAT","home":"https://www.emdat.be/","summary":"A cross-sectional analysis of the emergency events database from a pediatric perspective.\n\nThe international disasters database.\n\nDisaster group: Two main groups of disasters are distinguished in EM-DAT: natural disasters and technological disasters. This field is automatically linked to the disaster sub-group and the disaster type. There is a third group \u2018Complex disasters\u2019 which include some major famine situation for which the drought were not the main causal factor. See Table 1 for the Disasters Classification.\n\nIn 1988, the Centre for Research on the Epidemiology of Disasters (CRED) launched the Emergency Events Database (EM-DAT).","addition_date":"2020-01-14T09:31:10Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:30:09.683576Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:EM-DAT","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"}]}],"name":"EM-DAT","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/19012633","type":["Preprint"]},{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2020-046359","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Agricultural science","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3810"},{"term":"Database management","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3489"},{"term":"Ecology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0610"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"Public health and epidemiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3305"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:em-dat/db/www.emdat.be","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/19012633","p